---
import Checks from "../components/Checks.astro";
import InstallCommand from "../components/InstallCommand.astro";
import ProductFrame from "../components/ProductFrame.astro";
import ProviderFlow from "../components/ProviderFlow.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";

const description = "Flywheel pools every subscription you pay for, Claude included, and moves to the next account when one hits a cap. Its multi-agent workflows cost 30% less than Claude Code's on the same model, and one live session follows you from terminal to browser to phone.";
---

<SiteLayout title="Flywheel - Every subscription you pay for. One coding agent." description={description}>
  <SiteHeader />
  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <svg class="gauge" viewBox="0 0 560 560" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
        <circle cx="280" cy="280" r="238" stroke="oklch(0.28 0.012 185)" stroke-width="1" />
        <circle cx="280" cy="280" r="196" stroke="oklch(0.24 0.01 188)" stroke-width="1" />
        <g stroke="oklch(0.4 0.014 180)">
          <path d="M280 30v16M280 514v16M30 280h16M514 280h16" />
          <path d="M103 103l11 11M446 446l11 11M457 103l-11 11M114 446l-11 11" />
          <path d="M280 78v10M482 280h-10M280 482v-10M78 280h10" opacity="0.6" />
        </g>
        <circle cx="280" cy="280" r="238" stroke="oklch(0.78 0.13 75)" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="150 1345" stroke-dashoffset="-372" stroke-linecap="round" />
      </svg>
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="hero-inner">
          <p class="kicker">Open-source coding agent &middot; Apache 2.0</p>
          <h1>Every subscription you pay for.<br /><span class="dim">One coding agent.</span></h1>
          <p class="lede">Flywheel pools your Claude, ChatGPT, GitHub Copilot, SuperGrok, and OpenCode Go subscriptions, with as many accounts of each as you have. When one hits a cap, the next takes over without interrupting your work. Its multi-agent workflows cost 30% less than Claude Code's on the same model, and one live session follows you from terminal to browser to phone.</p>
          <InstallCommand id="install" />
          <div class="hero-links">
            <a href="https://github.com/wsauret/flywheel#install">Installation guide</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/wsauret/flywheel">GitHub</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="stage">
          <ProductFrame title="flywheel · relink">
            <img src="/media/hero.png" alt="The Flywheel terminal UI running a review workflow: five reviewer agents check a change at the same time" width="3064" height="1900" />
          </ProductFrame>
          <div class="stage-foot">
            <span><b>&gt;</b> one chat message: build &middot; review &middot; repair &middot; verify, then five reviewers at once</span>
            <span>Apache 2.0 &middot; macOS &middot; Linux &middot; Windows</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter" id="subscriptions">
      <div class="shell chapter-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">01 / Subscriptions</p>
          <h2>Two subscriptions? Flywheel uses both.</h2>
          <p class="body">Sign in to Claude, ChatGPT, GitHub Copilot, SuperGrok, and OpenCode Go, with as many paid accounts of each as you have. When one account hits a cap, Flywheel moves to the next one without interrupting your work. Add API keys for Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, DeepSeek, OpenRouter, or any OpenAI-compatible endpoint as a fallback.</p>
          <Checks items={[
            "The subscription whose weekly window resets soonest is used first, so quota about to expire is not wasted.",
            "Paid overage starts off, and Flywheel asks once per account before it uses it.",
            "Set a monthly limit on the GitHub Copilot credits that Flywheel uses.",
            "Claude signs in through Anthropic's official Claude Agent SDK. Flywheel never reads your Claude token.",
          ]} />
        </div>
        <div>
          <ProviderFlow />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter" id="workflows">
      <div class="shell chapter-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">02 / Workflows</p>
          <h2>Teams of agents. 30% cheaper.</h2>
          <p class="body">Describe the work in chat. For a big job, the agent launches a team of agents that build, review, repair, and verify, on any model, with independent work running at the same time.</p>
          <Checks items={[
            "A live card shows each phase and each agent. Open any agent to see its work.",
            "Open a helper agent to watch it work.",
            "Set a budget of tokens, minutes, or agent attempts.",
          ]} />
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="board" role="img" aria-label="Flywheel workflows against Claude Code's workflow mode on the same model and effort: 30% lower cost, 5% less time, and 22 wins, 11 losses, and 11 ties in blinded quality judging">
            <div class="board-head"><span>vs Claude Code &middot; <b>same model and effort</b></span><span>11 tasks &middot; 4 runs</span></div>
            <div class="zone">
              <div class="lrow"><span class="ev">cost</span><span class="det">30% lower</span></div>
              <div class="lrow"><span class="ev">time</span><span class="det">5% less</span></div>
              <div class="lrow"><span class="ev">blinded quality</span><span class="det">22 wins &middot; 11 losses &middot; 11 ties</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="board-foot"><span class="tick">&#9642;</span><a href="https://github.com/wsauret/flywheel/blob/main/bench/findings/workflow-audit-results.md">full results, method, and caveats</a></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter" id="surfaces">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="chapter-head">
          <p class="eyebrow">03 / Every screen</p>
          <h2>One session. Terminal, browser, or phone.</h2>
          <p class="body">Every client attaches to the same live session. Start a job in the terminal, follow it in the browser, and answer the agent's question from your phone.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="devices">
          <ProductFrame title="flywheel web">
            <img src="/media/web.png" alt="The Flywheel web client showing the same live session as the terminal" width="2880" height="1800" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </ProductFrame>
          <div class="phone">
            <img src="/media/phone.png" alt="The Flywheel phone client with a question from the agent waiting for an answer" width="1206" height="2622" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </div>
        </div>
        <ul class="facts">
          <li><b>Local web.</b> Open <a href="https://remote.flywl.sh/local">remote.flywl.sh/local</a> on the computer where Flywheel runs. It lists every project, open or asleep.</li>
          <li><b>Phone pairing.</b> <code>/remote</code> pairs your phone with a QR code. No account, no password.</li>
          <li><b>Free public relay.</b> Nothing to set up, and sealed end to end so the relay cannot read your messages. Or run your own relay on Cloudflare.</li>
          <li><b>Always current.</b> The phone runs the same client version as your computer, with no app update.</li>
          <li><b>VS Code.</b> The <a href="https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=flywheel-core-team.flywheel">extension</a> installs Flywheel for you, also on SSH hosts, and adds diff review with undo for each file.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter" id="scope">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="chapter-head">
          <p class="eyebrow">04 / Scope</p>
          <h2>It does what you asked. Nothing more.</h2>
          <p class="body">Scope creep and over-engineering are two of the biggest problems with today's frontier models. Flywheel is built to fight both.</p>
          <Checks items={[
            "No features, refactors, or \"improvements\" that you did not ask for.",
            "The simplest design that does the whole job.",
            "Every agent on a job stays on the plan that you approved.",
            "An agent says a change is done only after it has seen it work.",
          ]} />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter" id="models">
      <div class="shell chapter-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">05 / Models</p>
          <h2>The right model for every job.</h2>
          <p class="body">Instead of one model for everything, set a model and effort for the chat and for each kind of subagent, from any provider.</p>
          <Checks items={[
            "The model picker shows each model's price and which of your providers serve it.",
          ]} />
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="board" role="img" aria-label="One profile's model for each role: a strong model for the chat, a fast model for the explorer, and another provider's model for reviewers">
            <div class="board-head"><span>roles &middot; <b>one profile</b></span><span>model &middot; effort</span></div>
            <div class="zone">
              <div class="prow"><span class="name">chat</span><span class="accounts">Claude Opus &middot; high</span></div>
              <div class="prow"><span class="name">explorer</span><span class="accounts">Claude Haiku &middot; low</span></div>
              <div class="prow"><span class="name">implementer</span><span class="accounts">Claude Sonnet &middot; medium</span></div>
              <div class="prow"><span class="name">reviewers</span><span class="accounts">GPT &middot; high</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="board-foot"><span class="tick">&#9642;</span>$ /model</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter" id="profiles">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="chapter-head">
          <p class="eyebrow">06 / Profiles</p>
          <h2>Work and personal, kept apart.</h2>
          <p class="body">Bind each project to a profile. A work repository never spends your personal subscriptions, or the other way around. Make as many profiles as you like, each with its own signed-in accounts and model choices.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter" id="blocked">
      <div class="shell chapter-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">07 / Blocked</p>
          <h2>Know the moment an agent needs you.</h2>
          <p class="body">An agent only stops before completion when it needs your input or approval. Flywheel makes sure you see it.</p>
          <Checks items={[
            "In the terminal, the tab title turns yellow and the spinner turns into a ?.",
            "Your phone can notify you, and stays quiet otherwise.",
            "Everything that needs you stays in one Notifications list, also after a restart.",
          ]} />
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="board" role="img" aria-label="Three tabs in one terminal: two agents are working, and one waits for your answer">
            <div class="board-head"><span>tabs &middot; <b>3 sessions</b></span><span>one terminal</span></div>
            <div class="zone">
              <div class="lrow"><span class="ev">api-refactor</span><span class="det">working</span></div>
              <div class="lrow"><span class="ev wait">? docs</span><span class="det">waiting for you</span></div>
              <div class="lrow"><span class="ev">tests</span><span class="det">working</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="board-foot"><span class="tick">&#9642;</span>answer from the terminal, the browser, or your phone</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter" id="durable">
      <div class="shell chapter-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">08 / Durable</p>
          <h2>Close the terminal. It keeps going.</h2>
          <p class="body">Sessions are durable. They run in the background and continue after crashes, updates, and restarts.</p>
          <Checks items={[
            "Close the terminal, the browser, or the phone app. The session keeps running.",
            "Update Flywheel mid-run. Running builds and tests keep going, and agents continue on the new build.",
            "Out of quota on every subscription at 2 a.m.? The work pauses, then continues by itself when quota returns.",
            "After a crash, press Resume. Agents that were mid-task continue where they stopped.",
          ]} />
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="board" role="img" aria-label="An example night of one workflow run: the terminal closes, an update installs, the quota runs out and resets, and the run finishes verified">
            <div class="board-head"><span>one run &middot; <b>overnight</b></span><span>flywheel serve</span></div>
            <div class="zone">
              <div class="lrow"><span class="t">21:04</span><span class="ev">workflow started</span><span class="det">3 phases &middot; 5 agents</span></div>
              <div class="lrow"><span class="t">21:09</span><span class="ev">terminal closed</span><span class="det">run continues</span></div>
              <div class="lrow"><span class="t">23:40</span><span class="ev">update installed</span><span class="det">agents move to the new build</span></div>
              <div class="lrow"><span class="t">02:12</span><span class="ev wait">quota spent</span><span class="det">waiting for the reset</span></div>
              <div class="lrow"><span class="t">05:00</span><span class="ev">quota reset</span><span class="det">run continues</span></div>
              <div class="lrow"><span class="t">05:26</span><span class="ev ok">verify passed</span><span class="det">run complete</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="board-foot"><span class="tick">&#9642;</span>the run lives in the background service, not in the terminal</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter" id="learning">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="chapter-head">
          <p class="eyebrow">09 / Learning</p>
          <h2>It learns as you work.</h2>
          <p class="body">Flywheel remembers your preferences and turns what you teach it into skills that it uses next time. Every skill is a file that you can read, and <code>flywheel skills why</code> shows where it came from.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter" id="themes">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="chapter-head">
          <p class="eyebrow">10 / Themes</p>
          <h2>Your terminal, your colors.</h2>
          <p class="body">Flywheel ships about 40 themes, from Catppuccin to Gruvbox, and a new theme applies at once, with no restart. <code>flywheel font install</code> installs Monaspace, the font that Flywheel is designed around.</p>
        </div>
        <img class="themes" src="/media/themes.png" alt="Flywheel in three of its bundled themes" width="2880" height="736" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter" id="more">
      <div class="shell">
        <div class="chapter-head">
          <p class="eyebrow">11 / And also</p>
          <h2>Smaller things that matter.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="cards">
          <div class="card"><h3>Turn anything off.</h3><p>About 20 capabilities each have one switch. Keep only what you use, and the agent never sees the rest.</p></div>
          <div class="card"><h3>Many sessions, one window.</h3><p>Run as many sessions as you want in tabs in one terminal. <code>ctrl+n</code> opens a new tab, and <code>ctrl+s</code> finds any earlier session.</p></div>
          <div class="card"><h3>No account, no analytics.</h3><p>Flywheel collects no usage data.</p></div>
          <div class="card"><h3>Search every chat.</h3><p><code>/find</code> searches the text of this chat or of every chat in the project.</p></div>
          <div class="card"><h3>Measured speed.</h3><p><code>/stats</code> compares the measured speed of each model and effort.</p></div>
          <div class="card"><h3>Streaming diffs.</h3><p>File edits show as diffs while the model's response streams in, so you see each change as it is written, not after.</p></div>
          <div class="card"><h3>Long chats keep their details.</h3><p>After a long chat is summarized to make room, the agent can still find and reread the exact earlier text: an error, a file path, or the reason for a decision.</p></div>
          <div class="card"><h3>Your changes to built-in skills stay yours.</h3><p>When a new version ships, Flywheel asks whether to keep yours, take the new one, or merge the two. It never overwrites your work.</p></div>
          <div class="card"><h3>Chats can talk to each other.</h3><p>An agent in one chat can ask or answer another chat or workflow in the same project. You see each message in both transcripts.</p></div>
          <div class="card"><h3>Bring your MCP servers.</h3><p><code>flywheel mcp import .mcp.json</code> brings over the MCP servers you set up for Claude Code.</p></div>
          <div class="card"><h3>Fix it from the lightbulb.</h3><p>In VS Code, click the lightbulb on an error or warning to send that exact problem to Flywheel, or select code and ask Flywheel to explain it.</p></div>
          <div class="card"><h3>Free routes first, paid as backup.</h3><p>On OpenRouter and OpenCode Go, Flywheel can use the free version of a model first, and move to the paid route of the same model when the free one is not available.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter" id="get-started">
      <div class="shell install-final">
        <p class="eyebrow">12 / Install</p>
        <h2>Ready when you are.</h2>
        <p class="body">The installer verifies every download against the published SHA-256 digests. Flywheel then updates itself without interrupting a running session.</p>
        <InstallCommand id="install-footer" />
        <p class="matrix">darwin-arm64 &middot; darwin-x64 &middot; linux-x64 &middot; linux-arm64 &middot; linux-x64-musl &middot; linux-arm64-musl &middot; win32-x64 &middot; win32-arm64</p>
        <p class="matrix-note">On Alpine, run <code>apk add libstdc++ curl</code> before you install.</p>
        <p class="privacy">Flywheel agents run shell commands and edit files with your permissions, without asking before each step. Its guards catch ordinary mistakes but are not a sandbox, so run untrusted repositories inside a container, a virtual machine, or a disposable checkout.</p>
        <p class="privacy">For model inference, Flywheel sends your prompts and code only to the providers that you configure. Agent tools, such as MCP servers, web search, and shell commands, can send content to other destinations. Release builds send an automatic crash report with no conversation or file content. Turn off the Bug reports setting to stop it. <a href="https://github.com/wsauret/flywheel/blob/main/docs/privacy.md">What Flywheel sends over the network</a> lists every request it makes on its own.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
  <script>
    import "../scripts/site.ts";
  </script>
</SiteLayout>
